{"name":"Circus","hex":"#fc5e30","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Circus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Accipitridae – harriers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Circus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Circus","blocks":[{"text":"A circus is a company of performers who put on diverse entertainment shows that may include clowns, acrobats, trained animals, trapeze acts, musicians, dancers, hoopers, tightrope walkers, jugglers, magicians, ventriloquists, and unicyclists as well as other object manipulation and stunt-oriented artists. The term \"circus\" also describes the field of performance, training, and community which has followed various formats through its 250-year modern history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg/330px-Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus","wikidata":"Q47928"},{"title":"Circus (Britney Spears album)","blocks":[{"text":"Circus is the sixth studio album by American singer Britney Spears. It was released to coincide with her 27th birthday on December 2, 2008, by Jive Records. Transitioning from the \"darker and more urban\" themes of her fifth studio album Blackout (2007), Spears wanted to make her next project \"a little bit lighter\". She recorded much of the album between March and September 2008, after being involuntarily placed under a conservatorship earlier that year, following her highly publicized personal struggles in 2007. As executive producers, Larry Rudolph and Teresa LaBarbera Whites enlisted Spears' previous collaborators such as Max Martin, Bloodshy & Avant, Guy Sigsworth and Danja, as well as new ones, including Dr. Luke, Benny Blanco and Claude Kelly. Their efforts resulted in a primarily pop and dance record, whose lyrical themes addressed fame, infidelity, and infatuation."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Circus-_Album.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus_(Britney_Spears_album)","wikidata":"Q19345"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sells Brothers Circus with Great Danes ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChampion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astley's Amphitheatre in London, c. 1808","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAstley's_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Circus_Ronaldo_door_Dirk_Annemans.jpg/500px-Circus_Ronaldo_door_Dirk_Annemans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 